          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Keep track of the 'King of Hearts' (The Kingen). In the Kingen round, dumping this card on an opponent is the single most important tactical move.",
          intermediate: 'Strategic Leading: If you have a weak hand, lead suits where you have middle-rank cards (7, 8, 9) to force opponents to win tricks with their 10s and face cards.',
          advanced: "Void Management: Purposely exhaust your shortest suit early. This allows you to 'slough' (discard) your penalty cards (Queens/Hearts) safely onto tricks won by others.",
          tips: [
            "In the 'Last Two' round, count your 2s and 3s. You must save them to ensure you don't 'climb' into the 12th or 13th trick.",
            'Pay attention to the dealer; their choice of trump suit will tell you everything about their hand strength.',
          ],
